      "writtenOn": "2026-11-02T20:14:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This requires ownership of the buffer, but wouldn\u0027t the flow that we\u0027re looking at be something like:\n\n1. Process takes ownership, empties buffer, releases ownership\n2. Process takes ownership (currently fails because you can\u0027t take ownership of an empty wrap), repopulates, and then releases ownership?",
      "revId": "f8e6614304809a47c3d09bc5c311414a783e602a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "12b8107b_8dcfb023",
